meta {
  name: Describe Server
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.server.describeServer
  body: none
  auth: none
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
}

docs {
  Public server description. Returns the standard `com.atproto.server.describeServer`
  lexicon fields plus the off-lexicon `custos` extension object:

  {
    "did": "did:web:pds.example.com",
    "availableUserDomains": ["example.com"],
    "inviteCodeRequired": true,
    "phoneVerificationRequired": false,
    "custos": {
      "version": "0.8.1",
      "capabilities": ["sovereignSessions", "walletConsent", "didWebHosting"]
    }
  }

  `custos.capabilities` is derived from the running configuration, so a deployment
  advertises only what it can actually do (for example, `createCeremony` and `escrow`
  appear only when a master key is configured). Clients feature-gate on the presence of
  a name; a server that sends no `custos` object has none of these capabilities.
  `links` and `contact` are present only when configured.
}
